      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "[ RECHECK GMAIL / 1 unknown ]                 Apply: disabled\nRecheck reads labels; it does not replay the Archive request.\n\nAlready archived → confirmed. Still in Inbox → staged for explicit retry.\nUnavailable → remains unknown and locked against resubmission.\nA restart uses the recovery journal; never discard it to bypass recovery.",
      "originalText": "[ RECHECK GMAIL / 1 unknown ]                 Apply: disabled\nRecheck reads labels; it does not replay the Archive request.\n\nAlready archived → confirmed. Still in Inbox → staged for explicit retry.\nUnavailable → remains unknown and locked against resubmission.\nA restart uses the recovery journal; never discard it to bypass recovery.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "error-outside-note",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1840,
      "y": 1910,
      "width": 915.2,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#526175",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 51,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 151,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "Interaction annotation: the result view replaces the center/ledger, not the sender identity.\nSession receipts and recorded origins are proposed additions; do not infer old history.\nExisting outcome contract: triage.rs:203–232 and README “Write outcomes and recovery”.\nUnknown blocks new staging and Apply; failed items remain distinguishable and cancellable.\nThis is an error-state sketch, not a claimed 1100×600 pixel-fit validation.",
      "originalText": "Interaction annotation: the result view replaces the center/ledger, not the sender identity.\nSession receipts and recorded origins are proposed additions; do not infer old history.\nExisting outcome contract: triage.rs:203–232 and README “Write outcomes and recovery”.\nUnknown blocks new staging and Apply; failed items remain distinguishable and cancellable.\nThis is an error-state sketch, not a claimed 1100×600 pixel-fit validation.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "interaction-card",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#a8b9c9",
      "backgroundColor": "#f5f8fc",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 52,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 152,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "interaction-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 64,
      "y": 2134,
      "width": 811.2,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172b4d",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 53,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 153,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "PROPOSED INTERACTION / click, keyboard, membership\nClick sender or Enter on master → inspect; never check its messages.\nClick subject or Enter on member → preview; unread stays unchanged.\nSpace/Enter on checkbox toggles only that target. Mixed → check all eligible.\nAll/Pending tabs keep pending members visible but not eligible for restaging.\nExplicit Put back cancels their marks before they can be staged again.\n\nTab / Shift+Tab traverse master, subset tabs, checkboxes, actions, ledger.\nUp/Down navigate the focused list; focus outline is separate from preview.\nCtrl+F focuses loaded-message filter. Filter changes clear checkmarks.\nPROPOSED: changing sender/subset also clears checks, with an announced count\nin visible status; avoid hidden targets. This costs cross-sender convenience.\nA global matching-messages view can retain existing bulk selection scope;\nits group checkboxes must still name the represented eligible count.\n\nLedger subtotal → exact sender/action membership; origin line → explanation.\nEscape from expanded body restores member focus and scroll, not unread.\nCtrl+Enter outside text inputs uses Apply's same enabled/blocked state.\nRow menu retains Shift+F10 and row-local targets; never uses preview implicitly.\nDrag can remain optional: fully checked row = checked batch; otherwise row.\nDrop only stages; Escape/outside cancels. No hover-only path is required.\nThese are proposed interactions; keyboard or assistive-tech testing not run.",
      "originalText": "PROPOSED INTERACTION / click, keyboard, membership\nClick sender or Enter on master → inspect; never check its messages.\nClick subject or Enter on member → preview; unread stays unchanged.\nSpace/Enter on checkbox toggles only that target. Mixed → check all eligible.\nAll/Pending tabs keep pending members visible but not eligible for restaging.\nExplicit Put back cancels their marks before they can be staged again.\n\nTab / Shift+Tab traverse master, subset tabs, checkboxes, actions, ledger.\nUp/Down navigate the focused list; focus outline is separate from preview.\nCtrl+F focuses loaded-message filter. Filter changes clear checkmarks.\nPROPOSED: changing sender/subset also clears checks, with an announced count\nin visible status; avoid hidden targets. This costs cross-sender convenience.\nA global matching-messages view can retain existing bulk selection scope;\nits group checkboxes must still name the represented eligible count.\n\nLedger subtotal → exact sender/action membership; origin line → explanation.\nEscape from expanded body restores member focus and scroll, not unread.\nCtrl+Enter outside text inputs uses Apply's same enabled/blocked state.\nRow menu retains Shift+F10 and row-local targets; never uses preview implicitly.\nDrag can remain optional: fully checked row = checked batch; otherwise row.\nDrop only stages; Escape/outside cancels. No hover-only path is required.\nThese are proposed interactions; keyboard or assistive-tech testing not run.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-card",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 970,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#a8b9c9",
      "backgroundColor": "#f5f8fc",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 54,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 154,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "flow-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 994,
      "y": 2134,
      "width": 811.2,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172b4d",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 55,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 155,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "DECISION ORDER / preserve the safe write contract\nFixture before query: sender 20 = 10 undecided + 4 manual Archive + 6 manual Trash.\nOf those 10 undecided: 8 “Field Notes” Froms match R2; 2 F.N. Billing do not.\nRun query refreshes capped Inbox, stages those 8, keeps the existing 10 marks.\nAfter query: Archive 12 = query 8 + manual 4; Trash 6 = manual 6.\nR3 “Notes” also matches the 8, but R2 wins by list order, not specificity.\nRules do not target labels. No regex, priority scoring or new rule language.\n\nRule inspector shows list positions and full From examples beside members.\nNo implicit reordering. Editing an existing rule only saves the rule.\nNew sender-rule editor says “Save rule + stage matching undecided messages”.\nShow its literal From pattern and eligible count; do not imply all sender mail.\nNew provenance needs an explicit data-model addition; it does not exist today.\n\nStage → temporary intent. Apply → Gmail write. Put back → cancel only.\nUnsubmitted marks remain unsaved across restart; warn before discarding them.\nRead/unread → immediate write, independent of Archive/Trash and selection.\nOnly confirmed read results change local unread; uncertainty needs refresh.\nPreviewing pending/removed mail retains an explicit status and body.\nImages remain allowed by default per message, as in reader.rs:545–660\nand README “Reader and privacy”; blocking cannot undo sent requests.\nNo remote-image policy change is proposed here.",
      "originalText": "DECISION ORDER / preserve the safe write contract\nFixture before query: sender 20 = 10 undecided + 4 manual Archive + 6 manual Trash.\nOf those 10 undecided: 8 “Field Notes” Froms match R2; 2 F.N. Billing do not.\nRun query refreshes capped Inbox, stages those 8, keeps the existing 10 marks.\nAfter query: Archive 12 = query 8 + manual 4; Trash 6 = manual 6.\nR3 “Notes” also matches the 8, but R2 wins by list order, not specificity.\nRules do not target labels. No regex, priority scoring or new rule language.\n\nRule inspector shows list positions and full From examples beside members.\nNo implicit reordering. Editing an existing rule only saves the rule.\nNew sender-rule editor says “Save rule + stage matching undecided messages”.\nShow its literal From pattern and eligible count; do not imply all sender mail.\nNew provenance needs an explicit data-model addition; it does not exist today.\n\nStage → temporary intent. Apply → Gmail write. Put back → cancel only.\nUnsubmitted marks remain unsaved across restart; warn before discarding them.\nRead/unread → immediate write, independent of Archive/Trash and selection.\nOnly confirmed read results change local unread; uncertainty needs refresh.\nPreviewing pending/removed mail retains an explicit status and body.\nImages remain allowed by default per message, as in reader.rs:545–660\nand README “Reader and privacy”; blocking cannot undo sent requests.\nNo remote-image policy change is proposed here.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tradeoff-card",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1900,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 880,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#c8b48e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff8ed",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 56,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 156,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tradeoff-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1924,
      "y": 2134,
      "width": 811.2,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#624320",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 57,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 157,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "TRADEOFFS / intentional costs, not free improvements\n1. Stable sender identity vs faster disappearing work.\n   Keeping pending senders visible makes progress less visually dramatic.\n   Partition counts and an “undecided senders” view must prevent clutter.\n\n2. Provenance clarity vs model and recovery complexity.\n   Store decision-time rule snapshots, not just a computed RULE badge.\n   Recovery must tolerate missing origins; no fabricated historical reasons.\n   Session receipts must not become an accidental local mailbox or log of bodies.\n\n3. Single commit boundary vs expert throughput.\n   Removing Auto-apply adds Apply to quick Archive/Trash work.\n   Explicit “writes now” remains necessary for immediate read/unread actions.\n\n4. Sender-first navigation vs cross-sender bulk work.\n   Clearing checks on context switch is safer but breaks carrying targets around.\n   Keep an explicitly scoped global results route, rather than hidden selection.\n\nSMALL WINDOW DIRECTION / not a pixel-validated implementation\nAt 1100×600, use Senders / Members / Ledger as named workspace modes.\nKeep loaded scope and pending/recovery summary pinned; preserve sender ID.\nPreview replaces Members temporarily. No simultaneous three squeezed columns.",
      "originalText": "TRADEOFFS / intentional costs, not free improvements\n1. Stable sender identity vs faster disappearing work.\n   Keeping pending senders visible makes progress less visually dramatic.\n   Partition counts and an “undecided senders” view must prevent clutter.\n\n2. Provenance clarity vs model and recovery complexity.\n   Store decision-time rule snapshots, not just a computed RULE badge.\n   Recovery must tolerate missing origins; no fabricated historical reasons.\n   Session receipts must not become an accidental local mailbox or log of bodies.\n\n3. Single commit boundary vs expert throughput.\n   Removing Auto-apply adds Apply to quick Archive/Trash work.\n   Explicit “writes now” remains necessary for immediate read/unread actions.\n\n4. Sender-first navigation vs cross-sender bulk work.\n   Clearing checks on context switch is safer but breaks carrying targets around.\n   Keep an explicitly scoped global results route, rather than hidden selection.\n\nSMALL WINDOW DIRECTION / not a pixel-validated implementation\nAt 1100×600, use Senders / Members / Ledger as named workspace modes.\nKeep loaded scope and pending/recovery summary pinned; preserve sender ID.\nPreview replaces Members temporarily. No simultaneous three squeezed columns.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
